{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaSJuefyxsfBTayZhWsu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved `myLen_replicate`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\nThe proof works by induction on `n`:\n\n```lean\ntheorem myLen_replicate (n : Nat) (a : α) : myLen (List.replicate n a) = n := by\n  induction n with\n  | zero => rfl\n  | succ n ih => simp [List.replicate, myLen, ih]\n```\n\n- **When `n` is 0:** `List.replicate 0 a` is the empty list, and `myLen []` is 0 by definition, so `rfl` closes it.\n- **When `n` is `n + 1`:** `List.replicate (n+1) a` becomes `a :: List.replicate n a`, so its length is `myLen (List.replicate n a) + 1`. The induction hypothesis says that first part equals `n`, which leaves `n + 1 = n + 1`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":7861,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":439},"output_tokens":292,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e1e6db3-948d-4e83-9720-15decfc9944a","uuid":"9f85a5b5-4fa8-476a-b478-77359838b350","timestamp":"2026-10-31T14:01:25.590Z","request_id":"req_011CgaSJuRHQimBsjAp4fBwj"}
